# Netlify custom headers.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# The Thelo Android app bundles its HTML inside the APK, so the WebView runs the
# page from file:///android_asset/... . That gives the page the opaque origin
# "null", which means every fetch() it makes to this site is a CROSS-ORIGIN
# request and requires an Access-Control-Allow-Origin header on the response.
#
# The site used to be served from GitHub Pages (thelo.space), which sends
# "access-control-allow-origin: *" on every response automatically. Netlify does
# not. So when the site moved to Netlify (thelo.ink), the app kept rendering its
# whiteboard -- the HTML is local -- but silently failed to fetch any lesson JSON:
#
#     Access to fetch at 'https://thelo.ink/lessons/E1.json' from origin 'null'
#     has been blocked by CORS policy: No 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' header
#     is present on the requested resource.
#
# Images and audio kept working because <img> and <audio> are not CORS-restricted.
# That is why the symptom looked like "opens but content is missing" rather than
# an outright failure.
#
# This restores the behaviour the app was built against. It grants no new access:
# every file here is already publicly readable over plain HTTP.

/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *

# Web fonts are CORS-restricted even when referenced from CSS url(), so they need
# the header explicitly too. Long cache since these are content-addressed by name.
/fonts/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000

# Lesson content changes without the filename changing, so it must revalidate.
/lessons/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
